.\" Begin generated content:
.TH "SYD\-TSC" "1" "2026\-09\-01"
.PP
.SH "نام (NAME)"
.PP
\fBsyd\-tsc\fR \- Run a command without access to the timestamp counter
.PP
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.PP
\fBsyd\-tsc\fR \fI[\-h]\fR \fI{command [args.\&.\&.\&]}\fR
.PP
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.PP
The \fIsyd\-tsc\fR(1) utility runs a command without access to the timestamp
counter.\& Attempt to access the timestamp counter will cause the SIGSEGV
signal to be delivered to the process.\&
.PP
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.PP
.TS
l lx.
T{
\fB\-h\fR
T}	T{
Display help.\&
T}
.TE
.sp 1
.SH "وضعیت خروج (EXIT STATUS)"
.PP
On clean exit, \fBsyd\-tsc\fR exits with the same code as the child process.\&
On unclean termination, exit code is set to 128 plus signal number.\& In
case denying the timestamp counter or executing the child process fails
\fBsyd\-tsc\fR exits with the \fIerrno\fR(3) number.\&
.PP
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.PP
\fIsyd\fR(1), \fIsyd\fR(2), \fIsyd\fR(5), \fIsyd\-lock\fR(1), \fIsyd\-mdwe\fR(1),
\fIsyd\-ofd\fR(1), \fIsyd\-pds\fR(1), \fIsyd\-ring\fR(1), \fIsyd\-sec\fR(1), \fIPR_SET_TSC\fR(2const)
.PP
\fBsyd\fR homepage: https://sydbox.\&exherbo.\&org/
.PP
